From: gennro <gennro2004@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Input: retroid: check report length, hold the MCU off across sleep, retry its init

The status handler read 14 data bytes from any command-0x02 frame; a
short one that passed the checksum read its missing bytes as zeros,
which is a fully pulled trigger. Reports shorter than 14 bytes are now
dropped.

The driver had no PM ops: the MCU kept streaming across suspend, the
case rsinput's 1004/1311 fix for the same protocol (a geni RX interrupt
storm while the port stops, the IRQ disabled, a dead pad after resume),
and drew power all night. Hold it off (enable low, in reset) while
asleep and bring it back up from a work on resume.

The init sequence returned early on a failed or short write while probe
still succeeded, leaving a registered pad that never reported, and
nothing noticed an MCU that missed the sequence while still booting.
The sequence now fails on a failed write or when no report follows it
within a second, and the power-cycle plus sequence is retried from the
work, at probe as on resume. GPIO lookup errors fail (defer) probe
instead of leaving an ERR_PTR.

Buttons are reported whole from every report (no function-static
previous state to go stale across suspend), the triggers are clamped to
their range, and the ABS ranges are set by one helper. The axis layout
is unchanged: the triggers stay on ABS_HAT2X/ABS_HAT2Y, which ROCKNIX and
InputPlumber's Retroid maps expect, and the never-reported ABS_Z/ABS_RZ
stay advertised so SDL mappings and emulator configs keep their axis
numbers.
